cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use inazumaq2n in your work, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "inazumaq2n: a fast implementation of the Q2n image quality index"
abstract: >-
  A Python package that evaluates the Q2n hypercomplex image quality index
  for images with any number of bands from real moments of the blocks, with
  compiled kernels that are selected for the processor at run time and one
  matrix product per tile, without forming a hypercomplex product of pixels.
authors:
  - family-names: Lemley
    given-names: Harrison
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://git.tanuki-cd.com/algebraity/inazumaq2n"
keywords:
  - Q2n
  - image quality assessment
  - multispectral images
  - hyperspectral images
  - pansharpening
  - Cayley-Dickson algebras
  - hypercomplex numbers
